hile the room gathers around the hearth's glow. Use a landscape medium-wide frame at seated eye level from a front three-quarter view, with the face, both cup-holding hands, burning logs and nearby floor connected within the image. A natural 50mm perspective and moderate depth of field retain the material relationships, readable flame edges, lived-in wood and stone, and natural skin texture. The photograph feels observed during a private pause, with restrained grain and balanced highlights.",
